For all complex numbers $z$, let \[f(z) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
z^{2}&\text{ if }z\text{ is not real}, \\
-z^2 &\text{ if }z\text{ is real}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f(f(f(f(1+i))))$.

Put your final answer within \boxed{}.

Let $z = 1+i$. Then $f(z) = (1+i)^2 = 1-1+2i = 2i$. So $f(f(z)) = f(2i) = (-2i)^2 = 4$. So $f(f(f(z))) = f(4) = -4$. So $f(f(f(f(z)))) = f(-4) = 16$. So $f(f(f(f(1+i)))) = 16$.

The answer is: $\boxed{16}$.

